00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:55.755
Let's take a look at the different
types of reactions that we'll have.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:56.635
Okay.

00:01:56.635 --> 00:02:02.335
In front of us, we have D galactose, which
is a simple sugar or a monosaccharide.

00:02:02.845 --> 00:02:05.785
Now the whole thing that we're going
to be doing here is we're going to be

00:02:05.795 --> 00:02:10.315
first looking at how can this structure
change and how can we identify it?

00:02:10.875 --> 00:02:13.215
Now the first thing is, it's
all about naming, right?

00:02:13.225 --> 00:02:15.315
Naming an IUPAC is very important.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:18.675
So if we see that OSE ending
in the name, that's telling you

00:02:18.695 --> 00:02:19.984
that you have a simple sugar.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.830
We can see that ending up here
